meta {
  name: 31-Report a sketchy listing
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/listings/2/report
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "OFF_PLATFORM_FEES",
    "details": "The agent on this listing asked me to pay a ₦20k 'inspection fee' to a personal account on WhatsApp before letting me see the place. That's exactly the scam I came to DreamHomes to avoid."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 400, 401, 404, 409]
}

docs {
  Browsing other listings later, I came across one where the agent
  pulled the classic Lagos "₦20k inspection fee" line. Reporting
  it. Reason enum has SCAM / OFF_PLATFORM_FEES /
  STALE_OR_TAKEN / INAPPROPRIATE_CONTENT / OTHER — that's a great
  spread for the Lagos market. OFF_PLATFORM_FEES being its own
  category is exactly what we need.

  No "I want to be notified when this is resolved" toggle though,
  and no read-side for me to see what reports I've filed.
}
